From: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wmt: log the ftrace debug channel with pr_debug

osal_ftrace_print() wrote WMT's optional systrace markers with
trace_printk(). Any module that contains a trace_printk() call makes the
kernel allocate the trace_printk buffers and print the "trace_printk()
being used ... unsafe for production" notice when it loads, although
this channel is off unless the WMT debug interface turns it on.

Use pr_debug(): the channel stays available through dynamic debug, and
the module no longer carries a trace_printk format.
---
--- a/wmt_drv/common_main/linux/osal.c
+++ b/wmt_drv/common_main/linux/osal.c
@@ -1550,7 +1550,7 @@
 		va_end(args);
 
 		if (ret > 0)
-			trace_printk("%s\n", tempString);
+			pr_debug("%s\n", tempString);
 	}
 #endif
 	return ret;
